module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.derived_artifact_gate_blind_to_its_authority_merge

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data derived_artifact_gate_blind_to_its_authority_merge: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "derived_artifact_gate_blind_to_its_authority_merge" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "a clean merge of a roster deletes a row and every guard on its projection stays silent (THE GATE IS NOT WEAK HERE, IT IS ANSWERING A DIFFERENT QUESTION CORRECTLY, which is why this needs its own row rather than a stronger gate.",

    "Invalid state: an authority list whose members are appended by independent lanes in one lexical region, merged by ordinary text merge. Harm: git resolves adjacent appends by taking one side`s hunk, reports NO conflict, and the row another lane landed is gone from the authority.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable.",

    "WHY THE APPARATUS IS SILENT BY CONSTRUCTION, and this is the distinguishing fact. The document is DERIVED from the roster, so a roster missing a row projects a document missing that row and the generated-artifact gate is SATISFIED -- the artifact does match its authority. The refusing merge driver never fires either, because the conflict is not on the path it guards; it is one layer up, in the authority the projection is derived FROM. So a whole apparatus reports green while the loss passes through it, and silence from a mechanism that never applied is not evidence.",

    "RECEIPT, gunbc#10688 (2026-09-08). `dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode/roster.dag` auto-merged CLEANLY and wrongly: the branch appended three imports and three list entries in the region where main appended one, and `admission_roster_read_as_the_whole_membership_rule` -- landed by gunbc#10801 hours earlier -- was dropped along with its module file. Both merges reported zero conflicts. The head was pushed before the loss was found.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: wherever a roster of independently authored members is a plain list in one file, a clean merge is not evidence of coherence. The check is a SET DIFFERENCE AT MEMBER IDENTITY against the MERGE BASE, not against main -- missing relative to main mostly means the branch is behind, which is not a defect, while present at the merge base and absent on the branch is a deletion and nothing else. Do not substitute a count, a marker grep, or the artifact gate for it.",

    "A SECOND RULE, ABOUT THE CHECK ITSELF, because this class was almost missed twice. The set difference WAS run and DID print the missing row, beside an unconditional `echo` claiming the result was empty -- so a real finding rendered as its own refutation and a commit message asserted the opposite. A pass label that prints whether or not it was earned is a fabricated plausible output in a test oracle, DESIGN section 5. Branch on the result: emit the pass sentence only in the empty arm, and name the rows in the other.",

    "CEILING: 4, structurally impossible. Membership is decidable and the population is closed, so a roster that is a DERIVED join over the modules that declare a row -- rather than a hand-maintained list beside them -- cannot lose a member to a text merge, because there is no list to merge. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability: roster membership derived from the declaring modules, which is the same per-module declaration record `gunbc.declaration_index_seed_growth` owes and which several hand rosters already wait on.",

    "WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED: nothing here is repaired. The row that was lost is restored and the check is written correctly, but the roster is still a hand-maintained list in one lexical region and the next two lanes to append will meet exactly this merge. Measured at the time of writing: six open branches were behind main and had not yet integrated, each carrying the same append region.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
